## Overview

This configuration provisions the OCI networking required to enable Oracle Data Guard
between two Availability Domains (AZs) **within the same OCI region**.

| Resource | What it creates |
|---|---|
| `oci_core_local_peering_gateway.primary_lpg` | LPG on the Primary VM Cluster VCN |
| `oci_core_local_peering_gateway.standby_lpg` | LPG on the Standby VM Cluster VCN — immediately peered |
| `oci_core_network_security_group_security_rule` × 2 | TCP 1521 ingress rules on each NSG{% if add_ssh %} + SSH rules{% endif %} |
| `oci_core_default_route_table.primary_rt` | Route to standby subnet via Primary LPG |
| `oci_core_default_route_table.standby_rt` | Route to primary subnet via Standby LPG |

The two LPGs are **immediately peered** at creation (the primary LPG sets `peer_id` to the
standby LPG). This is a same-region operation — no DRG or Remote Peering Connection is needed.

