## Before You Apply — Import Existing Route Tables

The `oci_core_default_route_table` resources modify the **existing** default route tables
on your VM Cluster VCNs. Terraform must import them before applying, or it will replace
them and wipe any pre-existing routes.

```bash
terraform init

# Import primary VCN default route table
terraform import \
  oci_core_default_route_table.primary_rt \
  {{ primary_route_table_id or '<primary-default-rt-ocid>' }}

# Import standby VCN default route table
terraform import \
  oci_core_default_route_table.standby_rt \
  {{ standby_route_table_id or '<standby-default-rt-ocid>' }}
```

After importing, add any pre-existing route rules back into the `route_rules` blocks in
`main.tf` before running `terraform apply`.

---

## Apply

```bash
terraform init
terraform plan
terraform apply
```

Terraform creates both LPGs simultaneously and establishes the peer connection in a single
apply. The route table updates follow immediately.

---

## Outputs

After `terraform apply`:

```bash
terraform output primary_lpg_id   # OCID of the Primary Local Peering Gateway
terraform output standby_lpg_id   # OCID of the Standby Local Peering Gateway
terraform output peering_state    # Should be PEERED
```

